// Address layout for x86_64 user programs and servers.
//
// Phase D.3 closed Invariant #1: both programs (musl-linked and
// native sysl) and servers load into the high user carve-out at
// VA 0x60000000 (same `prog.ld` / `server.ld` shape as aarch64).
// Per-process VMA layout (code + stack VMAs) is the single source
// of truth — see `oskit/kernel/vma.lsysl::VMA_DEFAULT_*`. Initial-
// SP / stack-low values flow through `svc_vma_default_initial_sp`
// / `svc_vma_default_stack_low` (syscalls 96/97). The legacy
// `[0xCC000, 0x100000)` carve-out is gone; so are the
// `SRV_USP/SRV_SSP = 0xD4000/0xD3000` aliases that briefly stayed
// after Phase D.2 to ease RS's migration.
//
// PLATFORM_NAME (below) is the auxv `AT_PLATFORM` value — kept here
// because the prog build can't drag in cpu.lsysl's kernel externs.

module oskit.arch

// AT_PLATFORM string for the SysV initial stack auxv. ld-musl reads
// this via `__init_libc` -> `__libc.platform` and uses it to pick
// HWCAP-gated string routines. Must match what musl was built for —
// we cross-build x86_64-slix-linux-musl, so the platform name is
// the unprefixed arch name.
val PLATFORM_NAME = "x86_64"
